From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:50:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] virtual, signal: a no-access 4 KB page beside code faults
 inside its 16 KB host page

A 16 KB host page holds four 4 KB Windows pages and got the union of their
protections, so a committed PAGE_NOACCESS page beside an open one could be read
without a fault. World of Warcraft's x64 client keeps its code PAGE_NOACCESS and
opens it a page at a time when its exception hook sees the access violation; on
desktop Wine the code on Wow.exe+0x2DA000 reads a jump-table entry on the next,
still closed page, takes the read fault, and its hook opens the page first. On
the phone the read got the page's closed bytes without a fault and the client
jumped through them: Wow.exe+0x19575050, the value at +0x2DB590 in the file, at
two different image bases (runs 20261101T182709 and 20261101T184550).

A host page holding a committed no-access page (not a guard page) beside a page
with EXEC is now kept PROT_NONE by mprotect_range; the Mach exception handler
completes an access to its accessible pages through a transient alias of the
host page with the store/load emulators, and declines an access to the
no-access page, which then raises the guest's access violation as on x64
Windows. The decisions are in pp_noaccess_split.h (host test
tools/tests/test_noaccess_split.py).

Linear: PLA-516, PLA-514
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-01-wow-x64-fex.md
Offered-upstream: no; the 16 KB host page is the iOS port's
---
 build/ntdll-unix/pp_noaccess_split.h |  54 ++++++++++++++
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c  | 107 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 build/ntdll-unix/virtual_ios.c       |  52 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 213 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 build/ntdll-unix/pp_noaccess_split.h

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/pp_noaccess_split.h b/build/ntdll-unix/pp_noaccess_split.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c7359b7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/pp_noaccess_split.h
@@ -0,0 +1,54 @@
+/* Playport (PLA-516): noaccess-split host pages, the decisions virtual_ios.c and the
+ * Mach exception handler share (host test: tools/tests/test_noaccess_split.py).
+ *
+ * A 16 KB host page holds four 4 KB Windows pages and gets the union of their
+ * protections. A committed PAGE_NOACCESS page beside a page with (logical) EXEC is
+ * how a protector keeps its code closed a page at a time; reading the closed page
+ * from code on an open one must fault, as on x64 Windows, so such a host page is
+ * kept PROT_NONE and accesses to its accessible pages are completed through an
+ * alias. The bytes are Wine's per-page vprot; the PPNS_ values are Wine's VPROT_
+ * values (virtual_ios.c asserts it). */
+#ifndef PP_NOACCESS_SPLIT_H
+#define PP_NOACCESS_SPLIT_H
+
+#include <stddef.h>
+
+#define PPNS_READ       0x01
+#define PPNS_WRITE      0x02
+#define PPNS_EXEC       0x04
+#define PPNS_WRITECOPY  0x08
+#define PPNS_GUARD      0x10
+#define PPNS_COMMITTED  0x20
+#define PPNS_WRITEWATCH 0x40
+
+/* Is the host page made of these pages' vprot bytes noaccess-split: a committed
+ * page with no access (not a guard page) beside one with EXEC? */
+static inline int ppns_host_page_split( const unsigned char *vprot, size_t pages )
+{
+    int any_none = 0, any_exec = 0;
+    size_t i;
+
+    for (i = 0; i < pages; i++)
+    {
+        unsigned char v = vprot[i];
+        if (!(v & PPNS_COMMITTED) || (v & PPNS_GUARD)) continue;
+        if (!(v & (PPNS_READ | PPNS_WRITE | PPNS_EXEC | PPNS_WRITECOPY))) any_none = 1;
+        else if (v & PPNS_EXEC) any_exec = 1;
+    }
+    return any_none && any_exec;
+}
+
+/* May an access to a page with this vprot byte be completed through the alias?
+ * A read needs any access (EXEC pages stay readable, as for FEX's decoder); a write
+ * needs plain write (write-copy and write-watch keep their own fault paths).
+ * translator: the reader is FEX translating guest code (it holds its code lock),
+ * not the guest. A protection change that closes the page under it is followed by
+ * FEX dropping what it translated there, so its read of any committed page is
+ * completed, as the union protection did before. */
+static inline int ppns_page_allows( unsigned char v, int is_write, int translator )
+{
+    if (!(v & PPNS_COMMITTED) || (v & PPNS_GUARD)) return 0;
+    if (is_write) return (v & PPNS_WRITE) && !(v & (PPNS_WRITECOPY | PPNS_WRITEWATCH));
+    return translator || (v & (PPNS_READ | PPNS_WRITE | PPNS_EXEC | PPNS_WRITECOPY)) != 0;
+}
+#endif /* PP_NOACCESS_SPLIT_H */
diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 028f08b..9ed3da4 100644
